HASAGI Noncommercial License

Scope

This license covers the HASAGI PyTorch model definitions, native inference
and export code, the layers.pt and discernibility.pt checkpoints, the
Python inference package and its two ONNX models (layers_fp32.onnx and
discernibility_fp32.onnx), and the HASAGI Windows GUI, TUI and CLI
source, shared inference and reporting code. It also covers accompanying
HASAGI documentation, tests and build scripts. Together these are the
"Materials." Third-party materials retain their respective terms.

Noncommercial research and teaching

The HASAGI rights holders permit you to download, install, run, study,
and adapt the Materials, free of charge, solely for noncommercial
research or teaching. You may make working copies and fine-tune the
models for those purposes. You may publish research findings and share
a link to an authorized HASAGI download. Supplying copies of the
Materials alongside those findings requires the permission described
below.

Commercial use and redistribution

Obtain prior written authorization from the applicable HASAGI rights
holders or their authorized representative before either of the following:

  1. Using the Materials for a commercial purpose, including incorporating
     them into a commercial product or operating a paid inference service.
  2. Redistributing any of the Materials to another person or organization,
     in original or modified form, for any purpose, with or without a fee.
     This includes sending a model to a collaborator, mirroring a package,
     or distributing fine-tuned weights. The same rule applies to research
     and classroom distribution.

With any authorized redistribution, retain this license, the accompanying
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, and applicable attribution notices. Identify any
changes you have made.

Third-party rights

Each HASAGI rights holder grants permission only for rights they control.
Third-party material remains subject to its own terms. In particular,
the upstream Apache License, Version 2.0, and its notices are reproduced
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. Rights granted directly under those terms remain
available to recipients.

Warranty and liability

The Materials are supplied as is. To the extent permitted by applicable
law, the rights holders disclaim warranties, including merchantability,
